# Settings for Ollama Chat. Copy to .env and edit:
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# Why a file rather than `export` in a terminal: the app is started by the
# server manager, from an environment of its own, so it never sees your shell.
# This file is read by both — the app and the tools in tools/ — which is what
# makes `tools/check_web.py` passing mean anything about the app.
#
# Anything already set in the real environment wins over this file, so the
# server manager's program.env still overrides it and nothing here can pin a
# setting you meant to change for one run.
#
# Format: KEY=value, one per line. # starts a comment. Quotes are optional and
# one matching pair is removed. Nothing here is executed.
#
# The full list of settings is in the README's Configuration table; these are
# the ones worth setting on a new install.

# --- Where the model runs -----------------------------------------------
# Your desktop's LAN or Tailscale address if Ollama is not on this box.
#OLLAMA_HOST=http://127.0.0.1:11434
#OLLAMA_MODEL=llama3.1:8b

# --- Search --------------------------------------------------------------
# Strongly recommended. Unset means scraping DuckDuckGo, which works until
# your address is served a captcha, and then nothing gets past it. See
# searxng/ for a compose file that brings one up on this port.
#SEARXNG_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8888

# Small model used to turn a message into search queries. Unset reuses the
# answering model.
#WEB_PLANNER_MODEL=

# --- Access --------------------------------------------------------------
#CHAT_AUTH_USER=
#CHAT_AUTH_PASSWORD=
